 {:db/id "38c28c42-dcfa-5814-9aa6-882982c44e00"
  :question/id #uuid "38c28c42-dcfa-5814-9aa6-882982c44e00"
  :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 2 (question_59459020).\n\nLet $\\{\\vec v_1,\\vec v_2,\\vec v_3,\\ldots,\\vec v_k\\}$ be a set of vectors in $\\mathbb R^n$.\n\nIs the span of $\\{\\vec v_1,\\vec v_2,\\vec v_3,\\ldots,\\vec v_k\\}$ a subspace of $\\mathbb R^n$?"
  :question/answer-fields ["72185d4a-4342-50ef-a687-0b73470c2c19"]
  :question/worked-solution "Write $W=\\operatorname{span}\\{\\vec v_1,\\ldots,\\vec v_k\\}$. Choosing all coefficients zero shows $\\mathbf0\\in W$. If $\\mathbf u=\\sum_{i=1}^k a_i\\vec v_i$ and $\\mathbf w=\\sum_{i=1}^k b_i\\vec v_i$ lie in $W$, then\n\n$$\\mathbf u+\\mathbf w=\\sum_{i=1}^k(a_i+b_i)\\vec v_i\\in W,$$\n\nand for every real scalar $c$,\n\n$$c\\mathbf u=\\sum_{i=1}^k(ca_i)\\vec v_i\\in W.$$\n\nThese are the subspace conditions. The spanning vectors may be dependent, independent, or zero."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
