 {:db/id "a5aeec03-395c-5f4e-9e44-dc48d1a73d10"
  :question/id #uuid "a5aeec03-395c-5f4e-9e44-dc48d1a73d10"
  :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 3 (question_59459021).\n\nThe vectors in a basis for a subspace do not need to be linearly independent."
  :question/answer-fields ["e87ea751-8c30-5cab-a9be-b4aa1757ebf3"]
  :question/worked-solution "A basis for $V$ is a linearly independent set that spans $V$. Both conditions are necessary. For example, $\\{(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)\\}$ spans $\\mathbb R^2$ but is not a basis, because $(1,1)=(1,0)+(0,1)$ makes the set dependent."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
