 {:db/id "d54d5bea-6e03-5bed-9731-f246549d53f8"
  :question/id #uuid "d54d5bea-6e03-5bed-9731-f246549d53f8"
  :question/problem "Source question: Canvas Question 5 (question_59459023).\n\nThe standard basis of $\\mathbb R^n$ consists of the columns of the $n\\times n$ identity matrix."
  :question/answer-fields ["ce9720b3-74dc-5010-9cc5-2c2817621b31"]
  :question/worked-solution "The identity matrix is $I_n=[\\mathbf e_1\\ \\cdots\\ \\mathbf e_n]$. Its columns span $\\mathbb R^n$ because every vector $\\mathbf x=(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)^T$ equals $x_1\\mathbf e_1+\\cdots+x_n\\mathbf e_n$. They are independent because $c_1\\mathbf e_1+\\cdots+c_n\\mathbf e_n=\\mathbf0$ forces every coordinate $c_j$ to be zero. Thus these columns form the standard basis."
  :db/ensure :question/validate}
